OMNIA's changes to llama.cpp b11960 (commit 8642541) for cluster mode, applied by
scripts/build-llama-xcframework.sh with `git apply`.

build-xcframework.sh: builds the RPC backend (GGML_RPC, without RDMA) into the framework, so
OMNIA can spread a model over other devices and serve its own device to a cluster.

ggml-rpc: makes a lost worker an error instead of the end of the app. Upstream aborts the
process when a connection fails and waits forever on one that goes silent; a phone on Wi-Fi
does both when it locks or leaves. With this patch:
  - connecting gives up after 5 s, and a send or receive with no progress for 60 s fails;
  - sockets never raise SIGPIPE;
  - a failed connection completes every later command at once with safe placeholder answers,
    graph_compute returns GGML_STATUS_FAILED (so llama_decode reports it), and placeholder
    answers are never cached;
  - three functions, reached with ggml_backend_reg_get_proc_address on the "RPC" backend:
      size_t ggml_backend_rpc_failed_endpoints(char * buffer, size_t size)
      void   ggml_backend_rpc_clear_failures(void)
      void   ggml_backend_rpc_disconnect(const char * endpoint)
The wire protocol is unchanged (8.0.1), so official b11960 servers (ggml-rpc-server) work as workers.

